 "description": "Decide whether an API change breaks your clients, operation by operation. Compares parameters, request bodies, responses and security across two OpenAPI documents, and classifies each change by who it breaks: the clients that call the API or the clients that read its responses. A newly required parameter breaks callers; a widened response enum breaks readers. A change it cannot classify is never counted as safe. Pay 250000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
